# S4a: one of FIVE runs (S4a..S4e), each after its own all-four reset, of the AUDITS-OFF hang shapes on c2-packed-tp4-speed-strace-fcommit: the production recipe (audits off, the pinned sampler
# recorded in the verify trace, the tail caps) plus the fused commit. This is the allocation-order gate of docs/tp4-traced-publish.md (hazards 1 and 2): the fused commit adds about 68
# captures between the GDN commit traces and the request-engine builds, and production's trace shape is safe only by layout. FIVE CONSECUTIVE COMPLETIONS are the evidence; one stall
# restarts the count, stops the window and leaves the cards hung until the hand-back's reset. Read: every test completes, no stall-watch stack dump, '[PACKED-FUSED]' lines show the fused
# path engaged, '[PINDIAG] four-card engine programs=' deltas small after the captures, no late prefill program.
# STOP on a stall, a hang or a refusal.
# Duration (estimate): reset 1 to 3 min, build 10 to 20 min on a warm cache, the shapes 15 to 20 min: 40 min per run.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card tp4/next-3-scope window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-3-scope and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image a build-only job (C2_ACTIONS=build, no card opened) builds from this branch while
# production serves; a later commit of scripts needs a new build and tag. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-3m is a PLACEHOLDER the driver may substitute.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-3m
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-speed-strace-fcommit
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,long_real_text,concurrent4,concurrent4_v164order,concurrent4_steady,replay_concurrent4
